slides.content:
# In `getStaticProps` / `getServerSideProps`

The slug array is available in `context.params`.

```js
export async function getStaticProps({ params }) {
  const { slug } = params; // ['a', 'b', 'c']
  // use slug to fetch data
}
```

In `getStaticPaths`, you return paths as arrays:

```js
paths: [
  { params: { slug: ['2024', 'hello-world'] } },
  { params: { slug: ['2024'] } }
]
```

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/blog/[...slug].js
export default function BlogPost({ content }) {
  return <article>{content}</article>;
}

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  return {
    paths: [
      { params: { slug: ['2024', 'my-post'] } },
      { params: { slug: ['2023'] } }
    ],
    fallback: false
  };
}

export async function getStaticProps({ params }) {
  const { slug } = params; // e.g. ['2024', 'my-post']
  return { props: { content: `You are viewing: ${slug.join('/')}` } };
}
